    overview: "Oʻahu was home to powerful chiefdoms long before Honolulu became the capital of the Hawaiian Kingdom. Its harbors drew foreign traders, missionaries and later the U.S. military, and its city was where the kingdom was overthrown in 1893. Today it is the center of Hawaiian civic life, education and cultural revival.",
